  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Monascin may interact with CD276 antigen through a series of molecular pathways. Specifically, Monascin is implicated in targeting the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is known to be a target of Kanshone H, and this complex in turn targets CD276 antigen. Additionally, Monascin is also linked to the Phosphodiesterase 6C pathway, which is targeted by 5,6,8-Trimethoxy-2-Propylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, another compound that also targets CD276 antigen. These findings indicate that Monascin may exert its effects through multiple distinct molecular mechanisms, potentially influencing CD276 antigen through different pathways. The evidence is consistent across different scores, suggesting a plausible biological relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
